* 1.3.2, Sat Nov 7 2026
- Fix: embedded artwork now shows for AIFF and WAV files (it was never read from them), and for Opus files that store it as a picture block

* 1.3.1, Sat Nov 7 2026
- New: Retro skin: bevelled grey panels, push-in buttons and a black display with green text, a tribute to the desktop players of the late '90s
- Fix: .aif and .aifc files show in Add Files and are picked up when adding a folder (settings from older versions get them added)
- Fix: the tag editor says "4 tracks" instead of "4 track(s)"
- Fix: skin colours and fonts no longer leak into the tag editor (with the Retro skin its form area turned grey)
- Website: a Skins page showing all six skins; README has 1.3.0 screenshots

* 1.3.0, Sat Nov 7 2026
- New: Windows installer (TrackDeck-<version>-Windows-x64-Setup.exe): installs for your user without admin rights, Start menu shortcut, optional desktop icon and file associations, uninstall from Windows Settings; settings live in %AppData%\TrackDeck. The portable .zip is still available
- New: tag editor edits several selected tracks at once; fields that differ show "(various)" and are left alone unless you type in them
- New: tag editor fields for Key, Album artist and Remixer
- New: MP3 tags are saved as ID3v2.3 (what most DJ software reads), with ID3v2.4 as an option in Preferences
- Fix: the Label field is saved to the label tag (TPUB) in MP3s
- Fix: saving tags only changes the fields you edited; Serato and Traktor data, artwork and ratings are kept, and no ID3v1 or WAV INFO tags are added
- Fix: tracks on a drive that wasn't plugged in when TrackDeck started now fill in their details once the drive is connected
- Fix: the playlist updates straight after saving tags
- Change: the Apple Silicon download now needs macOS 15 Sequoia or newer (GitHub retired the macOS 14 build machines); older Macs can build with scripts/build-mac-macports.sh
- Website: Windows installer download; main macOS button says Apple Silicon M1+
- Build: the format test waits for playback to start instead of a fixed 6 s (it sometimes failed on a slow first launch on Windows)

* 1.2.1, Thu Nov 5 2026
- New: Intel Mac download (macOS 15 Sequoia or newer)
- Fix: the Khoshekh skin now follows the accent colour and the album-art background
- Build: scripts/build-mac-macports.sh builds TrackDeck on older Macs (e.g. macOS 12 Monterey) with MacPorts
- Website and README list the Intel download

* 1.2.0, Thu Nov 5 2026
- Fix: the app froze (beach ball) while tracks in iCloud Drive or other cloud folders downloaded; they're now fetched in the background
- Fix: a click with a slight mouse movement started a drag, which could hang with tracks on a disconnected drive and remove tracks from the playlist
- Fix: with Start paused on, the restored track showed "Drop music here to start" in the header
- Fix: a BPM detected while a track played didn't appear on the track info line
- New: playlists: Open Playlist (Cmd+L), Open Recent, Save (Cmd+S) / Save As (Shift+Cmd+S), and right-click Add to Playlist; .m3u8 files in ~/Music/TrackDeck Playlists; opening asks Replace / Add, with a default in Preferences
- New: detected BPMs are marked with * (e.g. 126.1*) so they can be told apart from tagged ones
- New defaults for fresh installs: Genre, Key and Label columns; Vivid waveform; orange accent; smooth-curve visualiser without peak caps
- Website: https://khoshekh-dj.github.io/trackdeck/

* 1.1.0, Wed Nov 4 2026
- New: live spectrum visualiser next to the track info (Modern and Khoshekh skins), with its own Preferences tab: style (bars, LED segments, mirrored, smooth curve), density, sensitivity, treble boost, fall speed, 30/60 fps, peak caps, colours
- New: BPM detection with aubio for tracks without a BPM tag (tracks under 15 minutes), cached so each track is analysed once
- New: sort the playlist by clicking a column header (numbers, durations, keys in Camelot order); a third click restores the previous order
- New: choose playlist columns in Preferences, including Genre, Key and Label
- New: waveform colour schemes (RGB, Vivid, accent colour) and an accent colour for the Modern skin
- New: album art as the window background (Modern skin)
- New: Khoshekh skin
- New: TrackDeck logo in the Metro, Silver and Slim skins
- Formats: WMA files now play in the packaged app; WavPack on Windows
- Modern skin: dark pop-up menus
- Fix: accented characters in tags (e.g. "Joaquín") showed as "?"
- Fix: the window opened off-screen if it was last closed on a display that's no longer connected
- Fix: Nulloy's name in window titles carried over from old settings
- Fix: leaked GStreamer messages
- Build: version is always current; build folders are created automatically; CI plays every supported format in the packaged app

* 1.0.2, Wed Nov 4 2026
- Fix: 1.0.1 builds reported themselves as 1.0.0 (About box, update prompts)
- Fix: white edge around the app icon in the Dock and on Windows
- CI: release builds fail if the tag doesn't match the version in ChangeLog/VERSION

* 1.0.1, Wed Nov 4 2026
- New: Windows build (portable zip, x64)
- macOS: Apple Lossless (ALAC), WMA, APE and other formats now play in the packaged app (FFmpeg decoders bundled)
- Build: Windows fixes (MSYS2/MinGW paths, folder creation, missing include)

* 1.0.0, Wed Nov 4 2026
- First release as TrackDeck (fork of Nulloy by Sergey Vlasov), with new name and icon
- New "Modern" skin, now the default
- RGB waveform coloured by frequency (bass/mids/highs), on by default
- Playlist columns from tags: Artist, Title, Album, BPM, Duration, on by default
- macOS: media keys, headphone buttons and Control Center (Now Playing)
- macOS: playback follows the default audio output (e.g. switching to Bluetooth headphones)
- Fix: blank global shortcuts hijacked the "A" key and could crash the app
- Fix: waveform elapsed/total label could show another track's length
- Fix: squashed playlist columns on a fresh install
- Self-contained macOS .dmg with bundled third-party licences, built by GitHub Actions

